+For every $n\ge1$ there is a reduced fan-out-two, rule-rank-two MCFG $G_n$ of
+size $O(n)$ with $\tau_{G_n}\le2$ and $\theta_{G_n}=O(n)$ such that the
+empty-component elimination stage of Proposition~\ref{prop:good-normalization}
+contains a retained nonterminal and a retained rule of thickness at least
+$2^n$.
+\end{proposition}
+
+\begin{proof}
+Let $G_n$ have nonterminals $S,A_0,\ldots,A_n$, with $S$ of fan-out one and
+the $A_i$ of fan-out two, and rules
+\[
+\begin{aligned}
+ A_0&\to(\mathtt a,\eps),\\
+ A_i&\to(\eps,\mathtt c)
+      \ \mid\
+      (\xi_1^1\xi_2^1,\,\xi_1^2\xi_2^2)(A_{i-1},A_{i-1})
+      \qquad(1\le i\le n),\\
+ S&\to(\xi_1^1\mathtt d\,\xi_1^2)(A_n).
+\end{aligned}
+\]
+The grammar is already nondeleting, nonpermuting, and nonmerging.  It is
+reduced: a rule at level $i$ can be placed on one branch of the binary rules
+above it, while all siblings use their shortest available derivations.  Every
+$A_i$ has a tuple of total length at most one, except that the start symbol has
+a shortest successful word of length two; hence $\tau_{G_n}\le2$.  The same
+one-branch construction shows that every source rule occurs in a successful
+sentence of length $O(n)$, so $\theta_{G_n}=O(n)$.
+
+Now consider a tuple of $A_i$ whose first component is nonempty and whose
+second component is empty.  The constant rule $(\eps,\mathtt c)$ cannot occur
+in such a derivation, because it contributes a terminal to the second
+component.  Consequently both children of the binary rule must have the same
+pattern recursively, and induction gives the unique shortest such tuple
+\[
+   (\mathtt a^{2^i},\eps).
+\]
+The pattern $\{1\}$ is therefore realizable for $A_n$, and it occurs in the
+successful word $\mathtt a^{2^n}\mathtt d$.  The empty-component elimination
+stage retains the decorated nonterminal $A_n^{\{1\}}$ and the projected start
+rule
+\[
+   S\to \xi_1^1\mathtt d\,(A_n^{\{1\}}).
+\]
+Every terminal tuple of $A_n^{\{1\}}$ has length at least $2^n$, so both this
+nonterminal and any successful use of the displayed start rule have thickness
+at least $2^n$.  Since the grammar is already nonpermuting and nonmerging, the
+remaining good-form steps need not alter this witness.
+\end{proof}
+
+The empty/nonempty component pattern is itself finite information.  Thus this
+example and Proposition~\ref{prop:typed-thickness-exponential} express the
+same general obstruction: a finite refinement of nonterminals may have a
+small source presentation while forcing exponentially long shortest witnesses
+inside one refined state.
 
